<p style="text-align: start;">
  Hello,
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  Welcome to GitHub for Startups! Your <b>$10,000 in platform credits</b> has been activated and applied to your
  <%= link_to @business_name, "https://github.com/enterprises/#{@business_slug}" %> Enterprise account.
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  <b>Next Steps</b>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  If you're currently on a trial, please <b>upgrade your trial Enterprise</b> (Enterprises &rarr; select your Enterprise &rarr; <em>Activate Enterprise</em>) to unlock the full product experience. <em>Please disregard the payment confirmation screen and select <b>&ldquo;Activate paid Enterprise.&rdquo;</b> Your platform credits will automatically begin to apply and you will not be charged until the credits expire.</em>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  <b>Tracking your credits</b>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  As an Enterprise account admin, you can monitor credit usage anytime in your Billing overview dashboard:
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  1. Navigate to your Enterprise's 'Billing and Licensing' Tab<br>
  2. Stay on the 'Overview' Tab<br>
  3. Click "More details" in the Current included usage tile
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  <b>About your credits</b>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  Credits are valid through <b><%= @credit_expiry_date %></b> and apply to metered products enabled on your Enterprise account including:
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  <span>&#8226; GitHub Enterprise licenses</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; GitHub Copilot Business or Enterprise (including premium features)</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; GitHub Advanced Security</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; Add-ons such as Larger Runners and Codespaces</span><br>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  Once credits are fully consumed—or once the 12-month program period ends—billing will automatically transition to the payment method on file. At that time, standard rates will apply to any products enabled on your Enterprise.
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  <b>Helpful resources</b>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  To help you get the most value from day one—especially with GitHub Copilot and GitHub Advanced Security—here are a few useful resources:
</p>

<p style="text-align: start;">
